  "final_message": "Done. The image gallery is complete and verified with 62/62 end-to-end API checks against gunicorn (the exact Dockerfile command).\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`, SQLite in `./data`):\n- Auth: `POST /api/auth/register` (201, 409 on duplicate), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 `{\"token\"}`), bearer tokens, 401 without a valid token\n- Images: paged `GET /api/images` (newest first, `page`/`page_size`, `{\"items\",\"total\",\"page\",\"page_size\"}`), `POST /api/images` (base64 `data` + `filename`/`title`, 201 with description incl. `url`), `GET /api/images/{id}`, `GET /api/images/{id}/file` (bytes unchanged + content type), `DELETE /api/images/{id}` (uploader only, 403 otherwise; removes row + file)\n- Format detection from magic bytes (PNG/JPEG only), duplicate filenames kept as separate images, image objects carry `id`, `filename`, `title`, `content_type`, `size_bytes`, `uploaded_at`, `url`, `uploader`; `/api/health` serves `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`; SPA fallback for non-API routes\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`, React + TS + Vite + Tailwind v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, `src/index.css` as Tailwind's entry):\n- Registration/sign-in forms, signed-in username + sign-out, responsive thumbnail grid (title-or-filename, uploader, date), paging + empty state, full-size modal with filename/title/size, upload form limited to PNG/JPEG with preview and API error messages, delete with confirmation on own images\n\n**Dependency fix**: the scaffold's `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` failed under pip 25 (hashes in a constraints file don't satisfy require-hashes mode), so `backend/requirements.txt` is now the complete pinned+hashed set from the lock \u2014 verified with the Dockerfile's exact command. `npm ci` + `npm run build` were also verified from clean.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
